<section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Who we are</h2>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        @PrivacyContacts.Controller, a building contractor based in Surrey, is the data controller for
        the information in this portal. Questions and requests go to
        <a class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover" href="mailto:@PrivacyContacts.Address">@PrivacyContacts.Address</a>.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What we hold, and about whom</h2>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        The portal is how we run each building project from first enquiry to final account, so it holds
        the people a project involves. What we hold depends on who you are to us.
    </p>
    <dl class="space-y-4 text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">Our staff and site operatives</dt>
            <dd>Your name, work email and phone number, the roles that decide what you can open, the
                days and hours you recorded on each site, your hourly rate and the cost of your time, sick
                and holiday absences, health and safety sign-in sheets and audit signatures, and a record of
                what you did in the portal (the audit trail). Where a site team runs a WhatsApp group for a
                project, its messages and photographs are imported into that project's daily record as
                written. Emails you send or receive on the projects mailbox may be marked against you as a
                measure of service to our clients.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">Our clients and the people who act for them</dt>
            <dd>Your name, email and phone number, the address of the works, the contract and its
                sum, the valuations, invoices and payments made under it, the variations and requests raised
                on it, and the emails and messages exchanged about it through the projects mailbox.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">Architects, subcontractors and suppliers</dt>
            <dd>Your company and the people we deal with there — names, emails, phone numbers and job
                titles — your insurance and compliance documents, CIS verification, the tenders, orders,
                invoices and defects between us, and the emails about them.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">People who ask us about a project</dt>
            <dd>Your name, email and phone number, the property the work would be on, what you told us
                you have in mind, the photographs of your home you sent through your private imagine page
                and the concept pictures we made from them, the estimate we prepared and any proposal we
                sent you. We keep a note of whether you asked us to keep in touch.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-content">Anyone who emails the projects mailbox</dt>
            <dd>Your email address, name and message, filed against the project or record it concerns.
                The portal reads the mailbox live; it does not keep a separate copy of every email.</dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
    <p class="text-content-muted leading-relaxed">
        Signing in sets one cookie, which keeps you signed in and nothing else. We do not use
        advertising or analytics cookies.
    </p>
</section>
